# Workflow and QA Rules

## Build & Deploy
- Validate build before deploy: `cd frontend && npm run build`.
- Deploy from repository ROOT (not `frontend/`).
- Pre-deploy: diff `frontend/dist/assets/index-*.js` bundle hash vs production. Stale bundle is the #1 cause of "works locally but not in prod" incidents.
- Rollback path: Firebase Hosting release history (`firebase hosting:clone`).

## QA Checklist (before marking task done)
- Region + sector switching tested across all 4 regions × 3 sectors.
- Async UI has both loading and error states — no silent failures.
- Responsive verified at 375, 768, 1024, and 1440 widths for UI-heavy changes.
- Heavy animation respects `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Color contrast meets WCAG AA (4.5:1 for text).
- No `console.log` left in frontend code (functions logging is allowed).
- No broken `href="#"` links.
- Adjacent pages that share components still work.
- When a page or shared component changed, finish from `frontend/` with `npm run lint`, `npm run build`, `npm test`, and `npm run e2e`. An unrun check is NOT RUN, never PASS.

## Mutual audit (2026-10-07)
- Cursor does the bulk implementation. Claude writes directives and audits Cursor's output.
- When Claude wrote the code, Cursor audits it from a `docs/directives/CURSOR_AUDIT_*.md` file. Audits are READ-ONLY: no fixes, no commits, no deploys.
- Audit reports follow `docs/AUDIT_REPORT_TEMPLATE.md`. An unrun check is NOT RUN, never PASS. Every FAIL needs a file path plus a line or key.
- Nothing is committed until the audit report is back and its blockers are closed.

## Deploy (2026-10-07)
- Cursor never deploys. Do not run `firebase deploy`, `npm run deploy`, or `gcloud`.
- Manual hosting: Oguzhan runs `npm run deploy` from the repo root.
- Automatic hosting: `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` on `main`, and only after `GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_PROVIDER` and `GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT` are set. Setup notes: `docs/CI_DEPLOY_SETUP.md`.
- Functions, rules, and indexes: Oguzhan runs the `firebase deploy --only … --project dynamicnfc-prod-68b4e` commands in `CLAUDE.md` §16.

## Where things live
- Directives: `docs/directives/`. Decisions: `memory/`.

## Languages (2026-10-06)
- Public site has five languages: en, it, fr, es, ar. Any new user-facing string needs all five.
- Page text lives in the page's `TR` object plus a sibling `*Translations.js` (it/fr/es). `npm test` checks key parity.
- Legal entity is exactly "NFC Software Systems Inc."; "DynamicNFC" is the product brand.

## Incident Protocol
F12 Console → capture full error stack → identify whether issue is frontend (bundle hash mismatch) or function (Cloud Functions logs) → rebuild + redeploy hosting BEFORE deep-diving into code.

## Large File Safety
When editing files >500 lines, verify integrity immediately after edit.
- PowerShell line count: `(Get-Content "path").Length`
- PowerShell tail: `Get-Content "path" -Tail 40`
- Bash equivalents: `wc -l <file>` and `tail -n 40 <file>`
- Confirm `npm run build` passes before considering the edit complete.